  "description": "# Sejong\n\n**SEJ · v0.4.0**\n\nCustom map of Sejong, Korea, built from official Korean government transport and demographic data.\n\n## Coverage\n\n<table style=\"width: auto\">\n<tr><td><strong>Region</strong></td><td>대전광역시, 충청북도, 세종특별자치시, 충청남도</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Playable Area</strong></td><td>1,610 km²</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<details>\n<summary>District list (13)</summary>\n\n<table style=\"width: auto\">\n<tr><th align=\"left\">시군구</th><th align=\"left\">District</th><th align=\"right\">Population</th></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"3\"><strong>대전광역시 (Daejeon)</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>대덕구</td><td>Daedeok-gu</td><td align=\"right\">233,379</td></tr>\n<tr><td>동구</td><td>Dong-gu</td><td align=\"right\">663,651</td></tr>\n<tr><td>서구</td><td>Seo-gu</td><td align=\"right\">400,006</td></tr>\n<tr><td>유성구</td><td>Yuseong-gu</td><td align=\"right\">409,697</td></tr>\n<tr><td>중구</td><td>Jung-gu</td><td align=\"right\">284,705</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"3\"><strong>충청북도 (Chungcheongbuk-do)</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>제천시</td><td>Jecheon-si</td><td align=\"right\">361,984</td></tr>\n<tr><td>청주시 상당구</td><td>Sangdang-gu Cheongju-si</td><td align=\"right\">85,452</td></tr>\n<tr><td>청주시 서원구</td><td>Seowon-gu Cheongju-si</td><td align=\"right\">158,480</td></tr>\n<tr><td>청주시 청원구</td><td>Cheongwon-gu Cheongju-si</td><td align=\"right\">48,188</td></tr>\n<tr><td>청주시 흥덕구</td><td>Heungdeok-gu Cheongju-si</td><td align=\"right\">227,467</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"3\"><strong>세종특별자치시 (Sejong City)</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>세종시</td><td>Sejong City</td><td align=\"right\">387,469</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"3\"><strong>충청남도 (Chungcheongnam-do)</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>계룡시</td><td>Gyeryong-si</td><td align=\"right\">7,404</td></tr>\n<tr><td>공주시</td><td>Gongju-si</td><td align=\"right\">80,014</td></tr>\n</table>\n</details>\n\n## Population Summary\n\n<table style=\"width: auto\">\n<tr><td><strong>Total Modeled Demand</strong></td><td align=\"right\">5,852,439</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Pops</strong></td><td align=\"right\">62,186</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n## Additional Features\n\n- **Neighborhood Labels** — The map includes municipal and neighborhood labels derived from administrative boundary data.\n\t- 시도 (Si, Do - Metropolitan / Provincial level)\n\t- 시군구 (Si, Gun, Gu - City / County / District level)\n\t- 읍면동 (Eup, Myeon, Dong - Neighborhood level)\n- **Special Demand POIs** — Airport, HSR station, Bus terminal, University, Hospital, School, Park, Shopping Center, Tourist Attraction, Ferry Terminal (where applicable); each modeled with real ridership, catchment gravity, or enrollment/visitor data.\n\n## Data Sources\n\n- Korean Transportation Database (Korea Transport Institute, KOTI) (ktdb.go.kr)\n- V-world (Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, MOLIT) (vworld.kr)\n- Statistical Geographic Information System (SGIS) plus (Ministry of Data and Statistics, MODS) (sgis.mods.go.kr)\n- Address-based Industry Support Service (Ministry of the Interior and Safety, MOIS) (business.juso.go.kr)\n- Aviation statistics 2025 (Korea Civil Aviation Association, KCAA) (airportal.go.kr)\n- Korean railroad statistics 2024 (Korea Railroad, KORAIL) (railstat.korail.com)\n- Korean Public Transportation Database (Korea Transportation Safety Authority, KTSA) (kotsa.or.kr)\n- Korean Hospital and Pharmacy Status (Health Insurance Review and Assessment Service, HIRA) (data.go.kr)\n- Health Insurance Medical Statistics (HIRA) (opendata.hira.or.kr)\n- Academy Information System (Ministry of Education, MOE) (academyinfo.go.kr)\n- School Info Disclosure (schoolinfo.go.kr) and Korea National Standard Data (data.go.kr) — schools, parks, shopping centers, tourist attractions\n- Korea Transport Safety Authority (KOMSA) coastal ferry statistics (komsa.or.kr)\n\n## Credits\n\nMap authored by budhakr",
